# Local MSBuild and helper outputs.
#
# These exclude directory CONTENTS (`/**`) rather than the directories
# themselves. That is deliberate and must stay that way: git never descends into
# an excluded DIRECTORY, so a plain `x64/Release/` rule makes every negation
# below impossible. If you re-tighten these to bare directory rules, the tool
# configs silently stop being tracked again.
src/build/win32/x64/**
**/build/win32/x64/**
**/x64/Release/**

# ...but the hand-ported tool configs ARE tracked, on purpose.
#
# These .cfg/.ini files are not build output - they are hand-authored or ported
# from the SOE reference tree, and the editors do not work without them. They
# carry the legacy no-sku TreeFile keys, the six ported SOE tool sections, the
# NpcEditor config work, and the [ParticleEditor] groundScene key that keeps the
# sky from rendering magenta. A clean checkout used to lose all of it.
#
# The intermediate directories must be re-included first, or git stops at them
# and never sees the files.
!src/build/win32/x64/
!src/build/win32/x64/Release/
!src/build/win32/x64/Release/*.cfg
!src/build/win32/x64/Release/*.ini
scripts/__pycache__/
mss64-stub/*.exp
deps/x64/lib/lgLcd.lib
deps/x64/lib/lgLcd_stubs.obj
